00:31:30,240 --> 00:31:31,560
And that is kind of tallied.

435
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:35,320
I mean, madly, the Girondins, they call for reprieve.

436
00:31:35,340 --> 00:31:37,020
They ask for another roll call vote.

437
00:31:37,320 --> 00:31:38,780
I mean, absolute madness.

438
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:40,360
And that, again, is rejected.

439
00:31:40,740 --> 00:31:46,680
So the final verdict is delivered three o'clock in the morning of the 18th of January.

440
00:31:47,240 --> 00:31:49,360
Bourne is a few hours off.

441
00:31:49,560 --> 00:31:57,140
And it's bad for the Girondins, because they now, again, they've kind of confirmed this sense among the Montagnards that they're closet royalists.

442
00:31:57,260 --> 00:32:03,000
But, of course, the person it's really bad for is the erstwhile king, Louis Capet.

443
00:32:03,600 --> 00:32:09,740
And so his lawyers, who have been standing the whole way through this vote, they haven't been given chairs.

444
00:32:10,060 --> 00:32:11,820
So it may be that...

445
00:32:13,060 --> 00:32:16,160
That fat bloke would have been in real trouble.

446
00:32:16,160 --> 00:32:17,380
Yeah, some justification.

447
00:32:18,340 --> 00:32:21,020
Anyway, they are allowed to give their response to the verdict.

448
00:32:21,280 --> 00:32:30,360
And Malzahar, who's a famous orator, gets to the tribunal, tries to give his talk, can't, breaks down in tears.

449
00:32:31,140 --> 00:32:33,700
You know, this is a tremendous display of sensibility.

450
00:32:34,040 --> 00:32:35,360
Everyone else is in tears.

451
00:32:35,480 --> 00:32:36,320
It's very Rousseau.

452
00:32:36,580 --> 00:32:39,840
And he then goes from the convention to the temple.

453
00:32:40,160 --> 00:32:45,260
He is led into the presence of the convicted criminal, Louis Capet.

454
00:32:45,700 --> 00:32:45,980
Yeah.

455
00:32:46,160 --> 00:32:49,560
And again, he tries to tell Louis what's happened.

456
00:32:49,760 --> 00:32:52,100
Again, he dissolves into tears.

457
00:32:52,500 --> 00:32:54,420
He falls at Louis' feet.

458
00:32:54,840 --> 00:33:00,080
And it's at Louis' feet that he announces the verdict of the convention.

459
00:33:01,280 --> 00:33:01,800
Death.

460
00:33:02,520 --> 00:33:04,180
Well, what a moving scene.

461
00:33:04,260 --> 00:33:12,640
And actually, I'm embarrassed, but moved, to report to the listeners that Tom actually can't continue because he, too, has dissolved into tears.

462
00:33:12,800 --> 00:33:14,200
So we're going to have to take a break.

463
00:33:14,500 --> 00:33:15,920
And we'll return.

464
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:21,000
We'll return after the break when Tom has regained his composure to tell you about Louis' fate.

